</address></addressbook></applicant><applicant status="new" format="epo"><addressbook><name>YAMAURA YUKIO</name><address><country>JP</country></address></addressbook></applicant><applicant status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>ASAHI KASEI KOGYO KABUSHIKI KAISHA</name></addressbook></applicant><applicant status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>HOSHI, SUSUMU</name></addressbook></applicant><applicant status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>YAMAURA, YUKIO</name></addressbook></applicant></applicants><inventors><inventor status="new" format="epo"><addressbook><name>HOSHI SUSUMU</name><address><country>JP</country></address></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="epo"><addressbook><name>YAMAURA YUKIO</name><address><country>JP</country></address></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>HOSHI, SUSUMU</name></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>YAMAURA, YUKIO</name></addressbook></inventor></inventors></parties></bibliographic-data><abstract load-source="docdb" source="national office" status="new" lang="EN"><p>A linear block copolymer comprising at least two vinylaromatic hydrocarbon polymer blocks (S), at least two conjugated diene polymer blocks (B), and at least one vinylaromatic hydrocarbon/conjugated diene copolymer block (B/S), characterized by having a specific block arrangement in which both terminal polymer blocks are blocks S, each of the blocks S has a block B directly bonded to its inner end, and each of the blocks B has at least one block B/S bonded to its inner end, and by being composed of at least two fractions having different peak molecular weights; and a resin composition comprising the linear block copolymer and a styrene resin in a specific proportion.</p></abstract><abstract load-source="docdb" source="national office" status="new" lang="FR"><p>On décrit un copolymère séquencé linéaire comprenant au moins deux copolymères blocs d'hydrocarbure vinylaromatique (S) et au moins deux polymères blocs de diène conjugué (B), et au moins un copolymère bloc d'hydrocarbure vinylaromatique et de diène conjugué (B/S). Le copolymère séquencé se caractérise en ce qu'il présente une disposition séquencé particulière dans laquelle les deux polymères blocs terminaux sont des blocs S et chaque bloc S comporte un bloc B directement lié à son extrémité interne, et chaque bloc B comporte au moins un bloc B/S lié à son extrémité interne. Le copolymère séquencé se caractérise aussi en ce qu'il est composé d'au moins deux fractions ayant un poids moléculaire maximal différent. On décrit une composition de résine contenant ledit copolymère séquencé linéaire et une résine de styrène dans une proportion spécifique.</p></abstract><copyright>User acknowledges that the Information Retrieval Facility (IRF) and its third party providers retain all right, title and interest in and to this xml under applicable copyright laws. User acquires no ownership rights to this xml including but not limited to its format. User hereby accepts the terms and conditions of the Licence Agreement set forth at http://www.ir-facility.org/legal/marec/data_licence</copyright></patent-document>